Basic Git Commands

Start

git init
git clone &lt;url&gt;
git status

Stage & Commit

git add &lt;file&gt;
git commit -m "msg"

Sync

git push
git pull

Branch

git branch &lt;name&gt;
git checkout -b &lt;name&gt;
git merge &lt;name&gt;

GitHub Workflow

Create a repository on GitHub
Clone locally: git clone &lt;url&gt;
Create a branch: git checkout -b &lt;branch-name&gt;
Make changes and commit
Push: git push origin &lt;branch-name&gt;
Create a pull request
Review and merge

Working with JSON Data
Convert a Python object into a JSON string:
import json

x = {"name": "John", "age": 30, "city": "New York"}
y = json.dumps(x)        # dict -&gt; JSON string

print(y)
# {"name": "John", "age": 30, "city": "New York"}
print(type(y))           # &lt;class 'str'&gt;

Caching for Speed
import pandas as pd
import time
import streamlit as st

@st.cache_data(ttl=600)
def load_sales():
    time.sleep(2)  # simulate slow IO
    return pd.read_csv("sales.csv")

@st.cache_resource
def get_bigquery_client():
    from google.cloud import bigquery
    return bigquery.Client()

df = load_sales()
st.dataframe(df.head())

@st.cache_data caches return values (data); @st.cache_resource caches singleton objects (connections, models).
